0.2.0 | 2026-11-19

  * Breaking: the plugin is now ICSNPP::MPLS (was Zeek::MPLSLogging).
    After upgrading a manual install, remove the old Zeek_MPLSLogging
    directory from the plugin path. Both versions register an analyzer
    named MPLSLogger.

  * Breaking: mpls_header.log field changes. experimentals is renamed
    traffic_class (RFC 5462). bottom_of_stack is removed; the last
    entry in labels is always the bottom of the stack.

  * Fix labels above 65535 being truncated to 16 bits. MPLS labels are
    20 bits, and Junos assigns dynamic labels starting at 299776.

  * Link mpls_header.log to the traffic it carries: uid, id, and
    is_orig of the connection the payload belongs to, plus
    src_l2_addr, dst_l2_addr, vlan, and inner_vlan from the frame that
    carried the label stack.

  * Summarize mpls_header.log by default. Packets that share a
    connection, direction, link-layer addresses, VLANs, label stack,
    and payload type collapse into one record per
    MPLSLogger::summary_interval (default 1 min), with new packets and
    last_ts fields. Set MPLSLogger::log_every_packet to T for one
    record per packet.

  * Detect the payload after the bottom label instead of assuming IP.
    Handles explicit NULL labels, IPv4 and IPv6, Ethernet pseudowires
    with or without a control word, and PW-ACH/G-ACh headers. ACH
    channels carrying IP are forwarded; other channel types are logged
    and not forwarded. The result goes in the new payload field.
    MPLSLogger::detect_payload turns detection off.

  * Record at most MPLSLogger::max_label_stack_depth (default 16) label
    stack entries. Deeper stacks are still parsed and raise an
    excessive_mpls_label_stack weird.

  * Resolve the record type, field offsets, and event handler once at
    initialization instead of on every packet, and skip building log
    values when nothing handles the event. Fix an off-by-one in the
    truncated-stack check.

  * Rename events: the analyzer raises MPLSLogger::mpls_header, and the
    log stream raises MPLSLogger::log_mpls_header.

  * Tests: synthetic traces for 20-bit labels and payload detection,
    and trace tests for 16 sample captures through
    testing/Scripts/run-mpls-trace. Remove the mpls.pcap test and its
    stale conn.log baseline.

  * Remove the "log writer" zkg tag, and update the zkg.meta
    description and template namespace.
